  1_problem: {
    **.style.text-transform: none
    _quality: {class: compiles}
    description: ||md
      # Generate Valid Angle Bracket Sequences
      Given `n`, return all valid sequences of `n` pairs of `<`\
        and `>` with proper nesting.

      ## Examples

      ### Example 1
      **Input:** `n = 1`  **Output:** `<>`

      With one pair, the only valid nesting is `<>`.

      ### Example 2
      **Input:** `n = 2`
      ```text
      <><>
      <<>>
      ```
      `<><>` places the two pairs side by side; `<<>>` nests the\
        second pair inside the first. Built by backtracking: add\
        `<` when fewer than `n` have been placed, add `>` when\
        there is an unmatched `<`.

      ### Example 3
      **Input:** `n = 3`
      ```text
      <<<>>>
      <<><>>
      <<>><>
      <><<>>
      <><><>
      ```
      5 valid sequences (Catalan(3)), analogous to balanced\
        parentheses `((()))`, `(()())`, `(())()`, `()(())`, `()()()`.

      ## Constraints
      `0 <= n <= 12`, `n` is an integer.

      ## Output Format
      Return a `STRING_ARRAY` containing every valid sequence of\
        `2n` characters.

      ## Function signature
      ```python
      def generateAngleBracketSequences(n):
          # accepts INTEGER n, returns STRING_ARRAY
      ```

      ## Sample Input/Output (from the page, ground truth)
      | | Input | Output |
      |---|---|---|
      | Sample 0 | `1` | `<>` |
      | Sample 1 | `2` | `<<>>`\n`<><>` |
    ||
  }
  2_err: {
    **.style.text-transform: none
    _quality: {class: compiles}
    description: ||md
      # HackerRank's "Input Format" section is wrong
      > The first line contains a single integer, n, representing\
          the total number of meetings. The next n lines each\
          contain two space-separated integers, representing the\
          `start_time` and `end_time` of a single meeting.
      >
      > ```text
      > 6
      > 1 2
      > 3 4
      > 0 6
      > 5 7
      > 8 9
      > 5 9
      > ```

      This is clearly boilerplate left over from an unrelated\
        meeting-scheduling problem (merge intervals / meeting\
        rooms) that HackerRank never edited after templating this\
        page.

      | | Input Format section (wrong) | Actual problem |
      |---|---|---|
      | first line | `n` = number of meetings | `n` = number of bracket pairs |
      | following lines | n lines of `start end` pairs | none - single integer input |
      | sample shown | 6 meetings, 6 lines of times | `1` -> `<>`; `2` -> `<<>>`/`<><>` |
    ||
  }
}
